## Session 51 Summary

**Major breakthrough: root-caused `tcp_dlm_scaling` (the criterion's primary blocker).**

**ROOT (PROVEN — captured 5+ min of live thrash dmesg during a stall):** `tcp_dlm_scaling` fails on a **symmetric PR→EX directory-inode upgrade livelock**. bash `open(O_CREAT)` does `lookup(dir PR)` then `create(dir EX-upgrade)`; both nodes cache PR and both want EX; the master `CONVBLK-DENY`s both with `-EDEADLK` (dlm.c:2574, without basting the conflicting holder); both self-demote PR→NL **through the bast_process durability drain** (`log_force(SYNC)` ~2s under cross-node contention) and re-collide. The ~2s clean-release drain is the livelock amplifier. (Saved: `sess51-ROOT-tcp-dlm-scaling-is-symmetric-PR-EX-dir-upgrade-livelock`.)

**Fix KEPT (build D50912EB, deployed both nodes):** durability-skip on clean **self-demote** releases (`mxfs_dir_pr_release_fast`, new `i_dlm_self_demote` flag). This kills the livelock amplifier without removing the coherency-masking barrier on genuine peer handoffs.

**Key empirical finding — the suite has a coherency-race CLASS, not one bug:**
- Broad skip (every clean release) → tcp_dlm_scaling **4/4 PASS** but exposes `dir_reuse`/`rsync_paired` ~17% (the clean-release log_force is an *incidental masking barrier* against the sess37/40 stale-block-RMW family).
- Self-demote-only skip → `dir_reuse`/`rsync` **solid**, but tcp_dlm_scaling still **~1/3 intermittent** (peer-handoff PR drains occasionally stall it).
- **Refuted** (both reverted): shortform-format gate (broke dir_reuse — its vulnerable phase *is* shortform sf→block growth) and an msleep node-slot tiebreak in the acquire path (cascaded to 12/17).

**Criterion NOT met.** The core tension: tcp_dlm_scaling needs clean-PR peer-handoff releases *cheap*; dir_reuse needs them *drained* (same code path). Next-session directions saved in `sess51-FIX-narrowed-self-demote-durability-skip-17of17`: (1) master-side proper conversion FIFO / deterministic winner in dlm.c (non-disruptive, unlike the requester msleep); (2) a true "no pending dir-data-block writeback" check (xfs_inode_clean only checks the inode, not data blocks) to make the broad skip safe; (3) fix the stale-block-RMW root directly (sess37 acquire-evict LOCKED-skip / sess40 writeback-skip owner-gone gap).

Code is in a clean, buildable state (D50912EB). I did **not** write the criteria-met marker — `./run.sh 2 tcp` is not yet reliably 17/17.

